@startuml sim_dotbot_mrta_ws_target_class_diagram

title sim_dotbot_mrta.py — target design: import MAPF_Simulation, own task allocation locally

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam classFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ClassBorderColor #4A90D9
skinparam ClassBackgroundColor #EAF4FF
skinparam ClassHeaderBackgroundColor #4A90D9
skinparam ClassHeaderFontColor #FFFFFF
skinparam PackageBorderColor #888888
skinparam PackageBackgroundColor #F8F8F8

note as N0
  Two independent targets on one diagram, reached in this order:
  1) WS-driven arrival (mrta_mode package) -- *implemented*, see the
     commit that extracted mrta_mode/ and AGENT.md's mrta_mode section.
  2) Retire the vendored simulation/ copy in favour of importing
     ~/3A/projets/MAPF_Simulation directly -- *not started*, the new
     part of this diagram. Its own algo/, mrta/, client/, report/ were
     removed upstream (deliberate refactor!s, see its TODO.md) -- only
     core/ and pibt/ remain, and pibt/PIBTPlanner is a different
     PathPlanner, not the old PIBTCoordinator. There is no upstream
     task-allocation layer left to import: FleetManager, QueueTaskSource,
     Task and the allocator all move from "borrowed" to "owned by
     mrta_mode".
end note

package "mrta_mode (WS-driven position, REST as fallback only -- implemented)" #E8F5E9 {

    class GridStateManager <<REST client — bootstrap + fallback only>> {
        + base_url : str
        + cell_mm : int | None
        + map_cells_x, map_cells_y : int
        --
        + fetch_dotbots() : list[dict]        <GET /controller/dotbots>
        + fetch_map_size() : (int, int)       <GET /controller/map_size>
        + set_map_size(width_mm, height_mm) : void
        + mm_to_cell(x_mm, y_mm) : Position
        + cell_to_mm(pos) : (float, float)
        + resolve_conflicts(positions) : dict[str, Position]
    }
    note bottom of GridStateManager
      No longer the step-loop's position source.
      Used once at startup (map size + initial bot
      list) and by ControllerStatusListener as the
      degraded-mode fallback when the WS link is down
      -- same GET /controller/dotbots as before, just
      off the hot path.
    end note

    class ControllerStatusListener <<new, replaces WaypointWatcher — WS client>> {
        + ws_url : str                         <ws://.../controller/ws/status>
        - _stop : Event
        --
        + start() : void
        + stop() : void
        - _listen_forever() : void
        - _handle_raw(raw) : void
        - _dispatch(notification) : void
    }
    note bottom of ControllerStatusListener
      Single WS connection, same endpoint as today.
      _dispatch() now reads *both* payload shapes carried
      by cmd=2 (UPDATE) instead of keeping one and
      dropping the other:
        - data.lh2_waypoints -> click_events queue
          (consumed by ManualClickTranslator, unchanged)
        - data.lh2_position   -> LivePositionStore.update()
          (new: was silently discarded before)
      Reconnect/backoff logic unchanged from WaypointWatcher.
    end note

    class LivePositionStore <<new>> {
        - _positions : dict[str, Position]
        - _updated : dict[str, Event]
        --
        + update(address, position_mm) : void
        + snapshot() : dict[str, Position]
        + wait_until_all_arrived(targets, timeout) : set[str]
    }
    note bottom of LivePositionStore
      Arrival is now event-driven: wait_until_all_arrived()
      blocks on per-bot Events set by update(), instead of
      DotBotNavigator's old GET /controller/dotbots poll loop.
      If no WS update arrives before `timeout`, falls back to
      one GridStateManager.fetch_dotbots() call -- same safety
      net principle as ManualClickTranslator.reconcile().
    end note

    class ManualClickTranslator <<unchanged>> {
        - _commanded : dict[str, Position]
        --
        + seed_commanded(dotbots_raw) : void
        + record_commanded(address, cell) : void
        + translate(waypoints_mm) : list[Position]
        + is_self_commanded(event) : bool
        + reconcile() : list[dict]              <-- REST fallback,
                                                      GridStateManager.fetch_dotbots()
    }

    class WaypointCommandClient <<renamed from DotBotNavigator — write-path only>> {
        + base_url : str
        + threshold : int
        --
        + send(address, waypoints_mm) : void          <PUT /controller/dotbots/{address}/0/waypoints>
        + send_all_parallel(moved_mm) : void           <N parallel PUTs, same route>
    }
    note bottom of WaypointCommandClient
      Arrival-waiting method removed: that responsibility
      moved to LivePositionStore, which already has the
      live data. This class purely issues commands.
    end note

    class MRTASession <<the "activatable mode" object>> {
        + engine : WorldEngine
        + fleet : FleetManager
        + queue_source : QueueTaskSource
        + adapter : TaskManifestAdapter
        + agents : list[Agent]
        --
        + start() : void
        + stop() : void
        + handle_click(address, waypoints_mm, source) : void
        + tick(step) : void
        - _cancel_agent_tasks(agent_id) : void
    }
    note bottom of MRTASession
      tick() now calls LivePositionStore.wait_until_all_arrived()
      instead of WaypointCommandClient.wait_until_all_arrived() --
      same call site, event-driven instead of polling.
    end note

    class MRTACli <<kept, thinned>> {
        --
        + main() : void
    }
}

package "MAPF_Simulation (external repo, imported -- core + pibt only)" #EAF4FF {
    class WorldEngine
    class Grid2D
    class Agent
    class Objective
    class AssignmentManifest
    class StepOutcome
    class PathPlanner <<interface>>
    class PIBTPlanner
    PathPlanner <|.. PIBTPlanner
    WorldEngine *-- PathPlanner
    WorldEngine *-- Agent
}
note bottom of PathPlanner
  Replaces the vendored simulation/ copy this diagram used to show as
  "unchanged": that copy is retired, this package is imported instead
  from ~/3A/projets/MAPF_Simulation (git@github.com:RasdaCorentin/
  MAPF_Simulation). No FleetManager, QueueTaskSource, Task, Allocator
  or PIBTCoordinator survive on the other side of this import -- see N0.
end note

package "mrta_mode (local -- task allocation, no longer covered upstream)" #FFF0F5 {
    class FleetManager
    class QueueTaskSource
    class Task
    class TaskManifestAdapter <<new -- design open>>
    FleetManager o-- QueueTaskSource
    FleetManager *-- Task
    TaskManifestAdapter ..> FleetManager
    TaskManifestAdapter ..> AssignmentManifest
}
note bottom of TaskManifestAdapter
  Replaces EasiestAllocator + the DispatchIntent wiring, neither of
  which exists upstream any more. Turns FleetManager's task queue into
  the AssignmentManifest of Objectives WorldEngine/PIBTPlanner expect
  per tick (goals bound to one Agent each, not a DispatchIntent keyed
  by agent_id). Exact shape is the open design question this
  reconnection forces -- not yet decided, deliberately sketched thin.
end note

MRTASession *-- GridStateManager
MRTASession *-- ControllerStatusListener
MRTASession *-- LivePositionStore
MRTASession *-- ManualClickTranslator
MRTASession *-- WaypointCommandClient
MRTASession *-- WorldEngine
MRTASession *-- FleetManager
MRTASession *-- QueueTaskSource
MRTASession *-- TaskManifestAdapter
MRTASession o-- Agent

ControllerStatusListener ..> ManualClickTranslator : click events\n(data.lh2_waypoints)
ControllerStatusListener ..> LivePositionStore : position events\n(data.lh2_position)

ManualClickTranslator ..> GridStateManager : uses (mm_to_cell,\nREST fallback)
LivePositionStore ..> GridStateManager : REST fallback only\n(WS outage)
WaypointCommandClient ..> GridStateManager : uses (cell_to_mm)

MRTACli ..> MRTASession : builds & runs (CLI driver)

@enduml
